// SUPERSEDED by abc-cluster-cli v0.1.80 (PR #62). This file existed because
// abc's generated head config declared queueSize = 50 and was passed with -c,
// which outranks the pipeline's own nextflow.config: the bound set there was
// silently ignored and five 6-CPU selections exhausted the node.
//
// v0.1.80 splits that generated config into an ENFORCED tier and an OVERRIDABLE
// defaults tier, and moves queueSize into the latter, loaded from $NXF_HOME/config.
// Nextflow reads that BELOW the pipeline's config, so executor.queueSize in
// nextflow.config now takes effect without this file.
//
// Kept, not deleted: it records why the bound is 3 on a single shared node, and
// it is still the way to override the value for one run without editing the
// pipeline. Passing it is harmless and now redundant.

// Concurrency for a single-node cluster, merged AFTER abc's injected head config.
//
// The pipeline's own nextflow.config cannot set this: `abc pipeline run` passes
// its generated nextflow.headjob.config with `-c`, which declares queueSize = 50
// and therefore outranks anything in the repository config. Pass this file with
// `--config` so it merges last and actually applies.
//
// Why 3: the cluster is one node shared with eighteen platform services. Five
// 6-CPU selections submitted at once exhausted its CPU, and Nomad's placement
// failure arrives as "[NOMAD] Cannot determine exit status" — a blocked task
// wearing a failed task's clothes — which Nextflow answers by retrying, adding
// more blocked allocations to a queue that is already full.
executor {
    queueSize = 3
}
